  "raw_text": "93\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Aiseya 36:22\n):\n \nai pr\nâ\nka nani ba kalkan\n \n–\n \nripped their clothing\n \n/ rasgaron su ropa)\n\nKalwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nKalkaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto rip, to tear, to mangle, to be ripped, to be torn, to be mangled, to wear out, to be\nworn out\n \n/ desgarrar, destrozar, desgastar\n\nKama\n \n(v-2p-fut of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(you) will be\n \n/ tú serás\n\nKamandanti\n \n(a/t:\n \nKamandante, Kamandant\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncommander, captain\n \n/ com\nand\nante,\n \ncap\nit\ná\nn\n\nKamisan\n \n(a/t:\n \nKomisan, Kumisan\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncommision\n \n/ comisi\nó\nn\n\nKamita\n \n(\nkm,lv,v\n-\n12/17\n;\n \nKomite\n-\ndict,dictu\n;\n \nKamita, Kumiti\n-\ndictu\n-\nalt\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncommittee\n \n/ comité\n\nLâka daukaia kamitika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \njudicial committee\n \n/ comité judicial\n\nSmalkaia Kamitika\n \n–\n \nTeaching Committee\n \n/ El Comité de Enseñanza\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nvi-12/17\n):\n \nSmalkaia Kamitika ra hilp mamunra\n \n–\n \nHelper to the Teaching Committee\n \n/ Ayudante del Comité de\nEnseñanza)\n\nKamna\n \n(v-1p-fut-II of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(I) will be\n \n/ seré\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-06/20-tnm-Impakan Sturka 3:14\n):\n \n“\nYang kamna dî\na kamna want sna ba”\n \n–\n \n“I will be what I want to be”\n \n/ \"Seré lo que\nquiero ser\")\n\nKampani\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncompany\n \n/ empresa\n\nKampani warkka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \njob, secular work\n \n/ trabajo, trabajo secular\n\nKan\n \n–\n \nfor, because\n \n/ por, porque\n\nKan\n \n–\n \nShort form of / Forma corta de:\n \nKaina\n \n(See\n \nKaina\n \nfor words with shortened form\n \nKan\n \n/ Ver\n \nKaina\n \npara palabras\ncon forma corta\n \nKan\n)\n\nKan kahbaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nKaina kahbaia\n\nKan\n \n(v-3p-past II of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \nwas, were\n \n/ era\n\nBri kan\n \n–\n \nwas having, had been\n \n/ estaba teniendo, había estado\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nyc-8\n):\n \n8 mani baman bri kan!\n \n–\n \n(He) was (having) 